WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:02.070
- Okay, so Quintessa, you are one

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:05.130
of the first non-binary
actors to play a superhero

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:07.440
in the DC universe, so
what does that mean to you?

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.510
It's gotta feel pretty cool.

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:13.110
- I think maybe I'm one of the first.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.710
I'm out, so that's one thing.

00:00:16.710 --> 00:00:18.360
There could be people who are questioning

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:22.200
or still figuring what that means to them

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:23.640
and their gender identity,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.723
but for me, I think it's an incredibly,

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:33.270
I don't take it lightly

00:00:33.270 --> 00:00:37.080
I think because as a young kid,

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.690
I never would've thought
that someone who's non-binary

00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:44.010
or trans could be open
enough with who they are

00:00:44.010 --> 00:00:47.070
and showcase who they are globally

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:51.330
and get far and be able to do the things

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:52.710
that they've always dreamt of

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.310
and just fully just embrace who they are.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.100
So I think being here and being out

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:01.140
and discussing these things

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:04.440
and even you asking that
question is so important

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:07.020
because there could be
a young trans person

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.760
or someone who's just questioning

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:11.850
who needs to see themselves represented

00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:13.410
in some sort of way just to know

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.710
that they can do anything
that they dreamt of.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:21.277
- Absolutely, inclusivity.
(audience cheering)

